{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 100)` priors for `sigma_a`, `sigma_b`, `sigma_beta`, and `sigma_y`. These parameters were already finitely constrained to `[0, 100]`, so the added statements make the implicit proper uniform priors explicit for SafeStan's unique-prior discipline without changing the posterior density. No data changes were required; `N`, `county`, `u`, and `x` remain unprotected context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=85> county;
  vector[N] u;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
transformed data {
  vector[N] inter;

  inter = u .* x;
}
parameters {
  vector[85] a;
  vector[85] b;
  vector[2] beta;
  real mu_a;
  real mu_b;
  real mu_beta;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_b;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_beta;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[county[i]] + x[i] * b[county[i]] + beta[1] * u[i]
               + beta[2] * inter[i];
  }
}
model {
  mu_beta ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_beta ~ uniform(0, 100);
  beta ~ normal(100 * mu_beta, sigma_beta);

  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  a ~ normal(mu_a, sigma_a);

  mu_b ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_b ~ uniform(0, 100);
  b ~ normal(0.1 * mu_b, sigma_b);

  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":1,"county":[1],"u":[3.270304434529317],"x":[3.5528982368417115],"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
